    "summary": "Cloth (probably a wrapper) formed of 7 strips of hand-spun white cotton, hand-sewn together along the selvedges. After assembling, the whole cloth has been stitch-tied with repeated blocks of three lines of chevrons, arranged regularly along each strip. The two outer strips have only a single block of chevrons; the five strips in the centre have two lines. The blocks are arranged to form bands across the cloth. The cloth has been dyed twice, once when stitched, and again after unstitching over the whole cloth. Along one end of the cloth is an extra pattern of two crosses on each strip.",
